# Source-derived semantics

- The source contains one instruction paragraph followed by one empty `div`.
- The `div` is 50px tall and uses `background: url("support/green_box.png");`; the shorthand is preserved verbatim because its image-only form is the assertion under test.
- The image uses the shorthand's initial repeat and position behavior to fill the box.

# Compatibility adjustments

- The paragraph is a Lynx `<text>` and the empty `div` is a `.test-box` `<view>`; the class-scoped selector avoids styling the generated `.body` wrapper.
- The card-local support image is copied without modification.
- `* { box-sizing: content-box; }` restores the Web sizing default.
- `.body { margin: 0 8px; }` and `.__ua-p { margin: 1em 0; }` reproduce Web body and paragraph spacing without relying on margin collapse. The page and content surface are explicitly white.

# Current Lynx API-doc basis

- `view` supports backgrounds and is the container for the test box; visible text must use `text`.
- The `background` shorthand and URL images are supported. Default Linear layout is vertical, and an unspecified child cross-axis width fills the parent.
- Lynx defaults to `border-box` and does not collapse vertical margins, so both differences are handled explicitly above.
